    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0856" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v15/pg824"/>

                <head>395. Editorial Note<anchor n="1" xml:id="d395-f1"/></head>
                <p>Substantial additional materials on Southeast Asia are in other volumes of the
                        <ref target="frus:frus1958-60v01"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi> series for the 1958–1960 period. Volume I</ref> is
                    devoted entirely to Vietnam. The East Asia regional compilation, which includes
                    considerable documentation on the Southeast Asia Treaty Organization, is in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1958-60v16">volume XVI</ref>, along with compilations on
                    Cambodia and Laos. A combined microfiche supplement to <ref
                        target="frus:frus1958-60v15">volumes XV</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus:frus1958-60v16">XVI</ref> has additional materials relating to
                    those three compilations and the entire selection of documents on Burma and
                    Malaya and Singapore.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
